# The ONE ignore file for the whole data layer. There are deliberately no
# nested .gitignore files under data/ -- if one appears, something below was
# not followed.
#
# DVC appends an entry to a .gitignore in the PARENT DIRECTORY of every output
# it adds or checks out, unless the path is already ignored: scmrepo's
# Git.ignore() early-returns on is_ignored(). Listing a chunk here therefore
# suppresses the nested file DVC would otherwise create for it.
#
# Three rules, all load-bearing:
#
#   1. NO TRAILING SLASH. git check-ignore matches "/reference/metabolism/"
#      against the directory, but DVC tests a bare path string with no trailing
#      slash, the dir-only pattern misses, and DVC writes the nested file
#      anyway. Measured, not assumed.
#   2. ONE LINE PER `dvc add` TARGET, added when you add the chunk. Forget it
#      and DVC recreates a nested .gitignore -- visible, not silent. The check
#      is: `find data -name .gitignore | wc -l` must be 1.
#   3. POINT AT THE LEAF CHUNK, NEVER A CONTAINER THAT HOLDS PINS. Ignoring the
#      container hides the .dvc files sitting inside it and they can never be
#      committed. This is why hosts/ is listed per host, not once.
#
# Only bulk is ignored. The pins (data/**/*.dvc), the curated tier, and the two
# tracked documents stay in git and must not be matched here.
#
# Tier rule (see build_references/REFERENCES.md):
#   raw/        acquired only -- a download or a licensed drop-in
#   reference/  compiled here, from raw/ only -- the direct refs
#   benchmark/  compiled here -- the evaluation set
#   curated/    hand-authored judgement, no producer. Small TEXT, git-tracked,
#               never a chunk -- so it appears nowhere below.

# -- scratch/ -----------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT a chunk and never `dvc add`ed -- the exception to "one line per add target"
# above. It is where the two build stages put their run directories: the staged
# input library, the agent home, per-step work dirs and results. Derived,
# transient, safe to delete. Listed here so a run does not fill `git status` with
# tens of gigabytes that nothing is ever meant to track.
/scratch

# -- raw/ ---------------------------------------------------------------------
/raw/hosts/e_coli_dh10b
/raw/hosts/e_coli_epi300
/raw/hosts/e_coli_k12
/raw/vector/pcc1.fna
/raw/kofam
/raw/metacyc
/raw/metanetx
/raw/rhea
/raw/uniref
/raw/kegg
/raw/equilibrator
/raw/literature/keio
/raw/literature/eydallin
/raw/literature/het_screen

# Not DVC-tracked: an upstream git checkout (bitbucket.org/jdwinkler/laser_release)
# pinned by url+sha256. Hashing a tree of git repos as data bytes turns its .git
# into thousands of cache objects and the checkout stops being a checkout.
/raw/literature/laser

# -- reference/ ---------------------------------------------------------------
/reference/hosts.fna
/reference/vector.fna
/reference/kofam
/reference/uniref50.dmnd
/reference/mnxr_lookup.parquet
/reference/metabolism
/reference/proteinBERT

# -- benchmark/ ---------------------------------------------------------------
# conditions.tsv (336 K) and Y/ (3.3 M) are small enough to stay in git, so they
# are deliberately absent here.
/benchmark/gpr.parquet
# hosts is a CONTAINER, not a chunk: one chunk per host, so the lines point at
# the leaf directories (rule 3). Ignoring /benchmark/hosts itself would hide the
# per-host pins sitting beside them.
/benchmark/hosts/e_coli_dh10b
/benchmark/hosts/e_coli_epi300
/benchmark/hosts/e_coli_k12
